# Backend Module Conventions

## Module folder contract

Each domain module follows this structure:

```
src/modules/<name>/
  routes.ts                   — Express router; auth and role middleware applied here
  controllers/
    <name>.controller.ts      — one file, or split by read/write if the domain warrants it
  services/
    <name>.service.ts         — one file, or split by read/write/responsibility
  models/
    <name>.model.ts           — Mongoose schema and TypeScript interface
```

Valid variation: controllers and services may be split into `<name>-read` and `<name>-write` files
when the domain has distinct read and write concerns (see `sick-leaves`, `vacation`, `praemien`).
This is a recognized pattern, not a violation.

## Controller responsibility boundary

Controllers do one thing: parse the request → call a service function → return a JSON response.
Business logic and database queries belong in services, not controllers.

## Multi-tenant enforcement

For the full companyId policy and the legacy-null fallback pattern, see:
`ambulancias-goruiz-backend/docs/POLICY-multi-tenant-legacy-companyId.md`

Utilities live in `src/utils/requireCompany.ts`:
- `requireCompanyForAdmin(req)` — use at the start of admin write operations
- `isSameCompany(targetCompanyId, adminCompanyId)` — use when a record may have a null companyId (legacy fallback)
- `isResourceFromCompany(resourceCompanyId, companyId)` — use for ambulances, hospitals, and other non-user resources
